chunks.text:
[Intro]
{a male Gregorian choir in unison, slow plainchant, stone cathedral reverb, no drums}
Con-fi-te-or...
{the choir holds one low note under everything that follows. A tired young man speaks over it, close to the microphone, slowly, every word clearly}
I wrote... tests.
{the choir answers, chanted}
Be honest.
{the young man, hesitating, clearly}
Okay. I RAN it. Once.
{the choir, lower}
Be honest.
{the young man, quietly}
I pushed it straight to prod.
{a calm, intimate female voice, very close, almost a whisper; then a reverse cymbal swell into the beat}
Thank you.

[Final Chorus]
{key change up, euphoric, the biggest moment of the song; the female voice sings each question}
{the crowd and the choir answer together, huge, triumphant}
Be honest: who wrote the tests?
I DID!
Be honest: who read the code?
I DID!
Be honest: who's still holding the candle?
{everything drops out; the tired young man alone, quietly, dry}
I did.
{the calm female voice, close, gentle}
Thank you.

[Outro]
{the male Gregorian choir alone, slow plainchant, cathedral reverb, fading, no drums}
Con-fi-te-or...
